# Holos content guardrails

The site content is the source of truth for the framework's positions: `Logic.tsx` for commitments, `Predictions.tsx` for tests and speculation. The history of each change, and why it was made, is in `wiki/log.md`. Canonical names for key terms, and the variants to avoid, are in `wiki/glossary.md`. Read the relevant section before editing it.

## Retired claims: do not reintroduce

- **Ordered dark matter** and everything built on it: Succession Nodes, the IDE-Pivot equation and "Succession Operator", dark energy as "fuel", DESI weakening as a signature of Succession, JWST COSMOS-Web mass peaks as nodes, axion-like particles as a substrate for "migration into the Bulk". Cosmological dark matter predates life (the CMB shows it) and outweighs all the ordinary matter anything could be built from. Dark Nodes are ordinary matter that has stopped shining: a trace population, a search channel and not a fingerprint.
- **Observation as selection, or as a constraint on earlier states.** Observation selects nothing, erases nothing, and changes no physics. Experience is lived inside observers; their causal pasts are lit; the rest remains unlit structure. Records are definite within each branch without observers (a detector's click included); an observer adds not definiteness but its being lived.
- **Born weights as shares of experience.** The weights are structural facts within C. For an observer they are self-locating odds: after a split and before looking, a branch's weight is your odds of being among its observers.
- **Branch counting as a measure, and weight as "the only measure left".** Branches and observers cannot be counted; counting gives an arbitrary or infinite number, and seventy percent of an infinite crowd is as large as thirty percent. Ruling out counting does not pick the replacement (the dartboard: odds depend on how the dart is thrown). Weight is the measure physics supplies: built into the state, conserved, unchanged by further splitting. The last step is a principle (Sebens and Carroll's epistemic separability), still debated. Gleason constrains the odds; never say it shows "consistency permits no alternative". Never say every observer's statistics follow the Born rule: observers with atypical records exist and carry almost none of the weight.
- **Theological and secular readings as interchangeable.** The monist reading is the framework's position.
- **"Falsified outright" for the standing bet, or a fallback that "leaves everything but Axiom 2 untouched".** Holos comes in two versions sharing one core (Axioms 1, 3, 4, 5): Holos without collapse, the version the site defends and bets on, and Holos with collapse, declared in advance (Predictions `#two-versions`). A consciousness-linked collapse would falsify Holos without collapse: Axiom 2's no-collapse reading, branching with self-locating odds, and "observation changes nothing it registers", which D6 and Axiom 3's "no change to any equation" carry only for that version. Axiom 4 survives: experience adds no force beyond the physics, which would then include a collapse law; never list Axiom 4 among the losses. In Holos with collapse, Omega is the universe with one history and lived, lit, and unlit apply within it; integration-tied collapse makes the threshold the collapse point (a Chalmers and McQueen style reading) and its strongest confirmation, while size-tied (objective) collapse leaves the threshold inert, gaining nothing. Declaring the second version does not make outcomes equal: a lost bet retires the defended version, and the other must earn its own support. Both versions lose through Test A. Never state "registration changes nothing" without tying it to the version defended here.
- **"Confirmed so far" for the standing bet.** No superposition tested so far has contained an observer. The bet is untested.
- **Omega as the ground of record agreement.** Physics secures agreement: the same signals reach observers who meet. Omega's one job is unity: every observer is the one subject, so crossing the threshold adds a place where it wakes, not a new self. Omega does not explain where waking happens; the threshold does, on any picture. Its payoff is philosophical, not experimental (see the Omega's payoff bullet below). Do not claim Omega explains why there is experience at all; the posits take experience as given.
- **The qubit observer-cut experiment.** Qubits register nothing below the threshold. Check C is a consistency check, not a test.

## Current commitments in brief

- Omega is physically the universe's complete quantum state: all branches included on the no-collapse reading (Axiom 2), a single history on a collapse reading. Never define Omega through Axiom 2, or the claim that Axioms 1, 3, 4, and 5 hold on any reading fails. Its existence rests on physics on any reading; what Holos adds is only that this whole is the one experiencer, which is interpretive and untestable. The title says "Bounded by Physics"; do not switch to "Grounded in Physics" until the threshold is measured.
- Five axioms make the framework: 1 Relationality, 2 Conservation (unitary, no collapse), 3 Threshold, 4 Two Sides, 5 Totality. Axioms 3 and 5 are the two additions to physics. The core is Axioms 1, 3, 4, and 5, which hold under any reading of quantum physics; Axiom 2 is the side taken on quantum physics and carries the declared fallback. Never call all five "the core". Commitments 1 and 2 are fundamental; Commitment 3 rests on Axiom 2. Every Proposition and Commitment names the axioms it follows from; Proposition IV (infinities) is a principle of method. Lived, lit, and unlit are definitions (D7).
- Two additions to physics: the integration threshold Φ_c, and the totality Omega as the one experiencer.
- Physics side: unitary, no collapse, branching. Relational QM is borrowed only for indexing registered facts to observers, not adopted.
- Observer requirements number four: integration (which includes feedback: parts constrain one another in both directions over time; never list recursion or causal autonomy separately), differentiation, temporal cohesion, and aboutness (the system's integrated states must carry a model of something beyond it: dynamics that mirror the structure of a world closely enough to generate, from inside, the kind of patterns that world sends in; the flight simulator versus the bank of light switches; any channel counts, including text, and channels may be open, gated, or gone, since a dream is the model running on its own; the requirement judges the machine, not the message, so a brain in a vat, Helen Keller, and a dreaming brain with its senses permanently cut all qualify). Never phrase aboutness as tracking the world "as it happens", as having a live channel, or as the world being able to drive or steer the system's range: a camera wired to every gate of an inert array passes that. Aboutness is structural, not historical, so "no dark duplicates" holds. It is what rules out high-Φ logic-gate arrays (Aaronson's objection), wired or not: they pass input through and model nothing. The notion of a model comes from predictive processing (Clark 2013), without its theory of consciousness.
- Axiom 4 (Two Sides) is dual-aspect: in an observer, experience and physical activity are two sides of one event. No dark duplicates holds in any possible world. Experience adds no force but is causally efficacious as the inside of physical causation; never describe it as a byproduct or as along for the ride.
- **Kind of view.** Holos is a two-sided monism with a threshold (Logic `#kind-of-view`): neither physicalism nor dualism. It agrees with physicalism that physics fixes every fact (copies match in every possible world) and differs on direction: physicalism grounds the inside in the outside, Holos grounds neither side in the other. The gloss is the curved line, concave from one side and convex from the other. Axiom 1 does work: a description built only from relations cannot state that a state is lived, which is why physics states experience only from outside. Never call Holos physicalism or dualism, and never say the inside is "produced by", "grounded in", or "emerges from" the outside.
- Incompleteness is in the description, not the world: physics fixes every fact but states it only from outside, and cannot say that any of it is lived. Never say physics misses a fact or that something exists beyond what it fixes; that would contradict no dark duplicates. The floor-plan example is the canonical gloss.
- AI: integration is measured where a system's causes are organized, whatever it is made of. Today's language models fall short of the threshold, as built (John, 2026-09-30, reversing the earlier "open question"): aboutness and differentiation are met, integration is not, because information runs one way within each step and the only top-to-bottom path is the output word. Always keep it architectural: a system built differently could cross the threshold, and nothing in Holos is specific to biology. Never say it lacks a world because its input is text. Fluency is never evidence either way.
- **Core line: "Reality requires a witness."** It is R = C ⊛ O in four words. "Reality" means lived reality (R) only. What physics produces, lived or not, is structure (C), and unlit structure exists as pattern but is never called real. The witness is an observer. Never let the line imply that a witness causes, creates, or changes structure: observation does not cause the universe, it makes structure lived. The early universe had no witness, yet is part of reality as the lit past that later observers' experience is about.
- ⊛ is ordinary composition: R = O(C(S)), "possibility, then registration", an order of logic, not time. Nothing exotic is claimed for the glyph. Never say C and O "constrain each other", "remain coupled", or form a feedback loop (not even "the loop between creation and observation"), and never call observation a process in time; in Holos without collapse, registration changes nothing it registers. R is the family of lived perspectives, one per observer per branch, each with the lit world it draws on. Iteration only follows one observer's thread. The Intro makes the point with no analogy: a universe complete as physics describes it, with no one in it, is real but not lived. Do not use the buffet (John rejected it, 2026-09-30) or the cookbook gloss (it makes unlived branches look like uncooked recipes, i.e. unreal). Creation is what physics actually produces from the universe's state, every branch of the one quantum state; never define it as every world the laws permit or say "every possibility remains". Worlds the laws merely allow from other beginnings are possibilities, not structure, and are not part of Omega. "Possibility" stays acceptable as the view from inside one branch: the others are its possibilities, and all of them occur.
- "Real": structure is fully real whether or not it is lived; R is lived reality, structure that is also lived. The difference is whether anyone lives it, not a grade of reality: never say "reality in the full sense", "actualized reality", "realized world", "real at two strengths", or call observation a "closure condition". The structure-versus-lived distinction is a starting point, not an explanation. Commitment 1 is "experience is local, and physics describes it only from outside" (local: only inside observers, never ambient or pooled in the whole; outside: the floor-plan gap); it rules out panpsychism, a cosmic mind, illusionism, strict physicalism of the "physical language can say it is lived" kind, and dualism. "Lived means experienced by an observer" is a definition, not a commitment. There is no Proposition V; its content lives in D7. Use "lived" for where experience occurs, "lit" for observers' causal pasts, and "unlit" for the rest.
- Three words, one meaning each, defined with "observer" (D7); "aperture" is the same system seen from Omega's side and belongs in Omega and monist-reading passages. **Lived**: where experience occurs, inside observers only; no one lived through the early universe. **Presence** is the noun for being lived (D7); write "lived", not "present as experience". **Lit**: binary, the causal past of at least one observer in its branch, the world experience is made from and about ("an observer lights its past"). **Unlit**: outside every observer's causal past (observer-free branches, beyond every horizon). **Witnessing**: graded, how much of the lit region experience is actually about. The old term "sealing" is retired in favor of "lit"; never say a region outside an aperture is "lived". Do not reintroduce branch-wide lighting "from beginning to end". Apertures cut off from one another are "walled off".

- **Claims box.** The Overview Introduction ends with "What Holos claims, and how firmly": physics as it stands; side taken on physics (two versions); side taken on mind (two-sided monism); first addition (threshold, Test A); second addition (Omega, untestable, payoff and price); hypothesis (genuine transition); companion ideas; speculation. Keep it in sync with the Claims section at the top of Logic (`#minimal-core`) whenever a claim's status changes.
- **Life's role.** The Overview's "Why Are We Here?" opens with it (the Meaning of Life section was merged there, 2026-09-28): life gives the universe a role, not a meaning; never promise more. Keep the role unlabeled and the "separation is not fundamental" reading labeled as speculation. Its one claim about value comes through Omega: joy and suffering anywhere belong to the one subject.

- **Words kept apart.** Detectors and records "record"; only observers "register". "Collapse" is reserved for quantum collapse and its ordinary senses; the Integration Hypothesis calls the fading of a civilization's signatures "Going Quiet" (formerly "Visibility Collapse"). Apparent retrocausality is record sorting after the fact, never "global self-consistency". Relativity "motivates" the block universe; never say it "leads to" or proves it. Proposition I concerns physical reality. Berkeley is an ancestor with one break (part of the whole is never lived); the Omega Point is never listed as convergent. Omega's existence rests on physics on any reading that has a universal state; relational QM and QBism deny one.

- **Revisions.** Retired claims are listed in `app/_components/Revisions.tsx` (the /revisions page, also in the PDF), oldest first; append new ones there, not in `Logic.tsx`. "Why Are We Here?" stays bold (John likes it): separation is not fundamental, labeled speculation, with entanglement (nonseparability) as its "why it is plausible". Never rest it on light's zero interval; state that only as a zero interval between two distinct events. One state is not one mind. Its answer is a role, not a purpose.

- **Closure (Proposition IV).** John holds this strongly: each higher description holds as a closed whole what the level below sees as endless or unfolding (Flatland's sphere; time flowing in 3D versus a history as one shape in spacetime; every branch held at once in the quantum state's space; Omega last, the description with nothing outside it). "There is no journey, there is closure." Never call it a ladder, rungs, or a climb, and never say "at the top": those make it sound like somewhere to go (retired 2026-09-29). Never frame it as places to go or as observers moving toward Omega (that revives the retired Omega-as-limit). "Higher description" and "one level up" are fine. "Closure" here means a higher description closing what a lower one leaves open; it never means observation as a "closure condition". Canonical home: Proposition IV; plain version in Overview Infinity; one pointer in Omega.

## Style

- Plain language for a general reader; gloss technical terms on first use.
- No em dashes; use colons, commas, or periods.
- **Omega's payoff.** "One subject instead of billions" is only a count; both pictures leave where and what to the threshold. Omega gives one answer, among serious rivals, to "why am I this one?" (nothing to explain) and the duplication puzzle (both are you); name the rivals fairly: Perry 1979 ("I" picks out whoever asks, like "here") and Parfit 1984 (identity is not what matters). Never say Omega "dissolves" or "settles" these puzzles, or that the many-subjects reading "leaves them standing" or is "weaker". Always state the price with the payoff: a stranger's future experience is as much yours to anticipate as your own; the walls keep you from feeling it, not from being the one who will. That price is also the ethical point: self-interest and concern for others coincide. Not unique: Parfit reached similar impartiality without one subject. The threshold and Axiom 4 do not depend on Omega. Name the view open individualism (Kolak). Never claim Omega explains where or what experience is.
- **"Fundamental" experience.** Means underived (the fact Holos starts from), never "everywhere" or "free of physics". Proposition I and Axiom 1 do not reach experience.
- **Threshold strength.** The threshold is three claims of different strength (Logic `#threshold-claims`): (1) Edge: clear cases on both sides and a narrow twilight between, where there is no exact fact; part of Axiom 3. (2) Integration: integration plus the other requirements carries a system across; the core claim, lost only through Test A. (3) Transition: the crossing is a genuine transition, abrupt or continuous, not an arbitrary stretch of a smooth slope; hypothesis. Holos takes no side on which kind (John, 2026-09-28), so never call the crossing a "critical transition" or "critical point": those name the continuous kind only. "Critical point" stays correct for waking cortex's operating point. Its prediction: the twilight narrows as systems grow (finite-size scaling), so brains cross steeply and small systems have wide twilights; the cheapest test is dish-grown networks of different sizes (Predictions Test B, `#minimal-neural-systems`), with claim 3 lost if steepness does not grow with size. If claim 3 fails, the core stands and the twilight is wider. Retired 2026-09-28: one shared shape (universality class) for every crossing, and one universal Φ_c value; John does not hold them, nothing in Holos implies them, and physics expects systems differing in geometry and wiring to cross differently. Never reintroduce them. Never say presence is binary, that there is "no halfway state", or that an exact line exists in a finite system: exact lines exist only in infinite systems, which Proposition IV reads as model limits. Never call "graded presence" a way to lose. Where the twilight falls is fixed by structure in every possible world (the percolation image: the crossing point is fixed by the grid, whatever the pipes are made of), so a copy of a borderline system is borderline too; never call the threshold a contingent constant of nature. Holos rejects the no-vagueness premise (Antony) with Schwitzgebel's reply; clear cases stay clear, so the twilight is not panpsychism. Integration is the result, not the knob: conditions (wiring, development, drug level) move it; Φ ≥ Φ_c is shorthand for past the twilight. Near-criticality of waking cortex (Toker 2022, avalanches, the 2024 EEG study) marks the operating point, where differentiation and richness peak, not the threshold; never cite it as evidence for claim 3. Seizures are joined but not varied (differentiation fails); psychedelics move cortex closer to criticality. Toker studied waking, generalized seizure, anesthesia, psychedelics, and disorders of consciousness, not deep sleep. Neural inertia (hysteresis) fits claim 3 as an abrupt switch, but in flies sleep genes control it (Joiner 2013), so it may belong to the arousal switch; human evidence is mixed (Kuizenga 2018: none with propofol, some with sevoflurane). Do not use water freezing as the threshold analogy; use the Curie point. Water freezing is fine as an example of the sudden kind of switch.
- **Test A protocol.** Frozen gauges: PCI (TMS-EEG) with the published 0.31 cutoff (Casarotto 2016) as primary; a posterior-cortex gauge named in advance, its cutoff set on calibration states and frozen before held-out data. Timing: gauges end at the awakening; reports count only for what was happening just before waking. A failing gauge is discarded, not Holos; Holos loses if, across independent studies, detailed reports reliably come from periods when both gauges sat clearly below their frozen cutoffs. No gauge proposed afterward can rescue results already in. The local reply to NREM dreaming was adopted after Siclari 2017 and Nieminen 2016, so those data never count in Holos's favor. Report the evidence both ways: Bajwa 2025 (the nearest test, no difference, timing-limited) and Aamodt 2022 against; Nieminen 2016 and Siclari 2017 for. Never say "positive reports are unaffected"; they escape the memory confound, not the timing one.
- **Unlit examples.** Use aperture-free branches and regions beyond every observer's horizon. Never cite "the far future after the last observer": fluctuation observers (Boltzmann brains) in some branch could light it.
- **Born odds under monism.** Self-locating uncertainty belongs to each walled-off aperture, not to Omega. Keep "why am I this one?" (a reason, dissolved by monism) apart from "which one is this?" (information, answered by the Born odds).
- **Describing language models.** Information flows up through layers and forward in time at each level via stored notes (the KV cache) that later steps read but never rewrite; the only top-to-bottom path is the output word. Never say the loop is "only one word wide".
- **Star-level waste heat.** The Integration Hypothesis points to single stars warm in the infrared, not galaxies. As of 2026-09-26 the Hephaistos candidates are mostly traced or suspected to be background galaxies; never present them as live technosignatures.
- **Omega is not a limit.** Omega is the whole, existing now: physically the universal quantum state, experientially the one experiencer. Never call it a limit, endpoint, or horizon finite systems approach, never say deeper integration witnesses "more of" the whole or brings an observer nearer it, and never say it is fully registered or fully integrated ("nothing unregistered"): unlit structure is part of it and never lived. Say "Omega", not "the Omega Point", except when naming Teilhard or Tipler. Omega is the ultimate whole, not the ultimate integration: everything is in it, all at once, but its parts are not all joined. Never exempt Omega from maximality as "not a system among systems" or a "category mistake"; the reason it is never a peak is physical: the whole splits into parts that never touch (regions beyond each other's horizons), so its integration is near zero. Never cite branches as a seam: branches are not parts, so no integration measure cuts there. This also explains why it pools nothing. Its Logic material lives in the core section `#totality`.
- **Integration Hypothesis assumptions.** Keep it bold but name its bet: motives converge, so nearly every civilization and independent colony turns inward before founding more than one new settlement; the reason is that light-speed delay and waste heat press on all alike. Physics does not guarantee it; independence can speed spreading; settlement models (Carroll-Nellenback et al. 2019) make the outcome turn on rates. The Jevons reply is also a bet about motives (new minds stay near their makers). Heat: say long-running computers shed heat because error correction erases information (Landauer 1961), never "anything that computes must shed heat" flatly. The radiator loophole is narrowed, not closed: a radiator needs no integration, so avoiding vast cold radiators is a bet about preference.
- **Speculation standard.** Every item in Speculation must be physically possible, not extremely unlikely, and carry a "Why it is plausible" note grounded in known physics or published work. Modify or remove anything that fails. Never restate the Teeming Dark or Aliens there; point to them.
